<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Update on HEUSSER.PRO</title><link>https://heusser.pro/categories/update/</link><description>Recent content in Update on HEUSSER.PRO</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 29 Sep 2022 20:31:53 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://heusser.pro/categories/update/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Updated Calling UI on Teams Desk Phones</title><link>https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/</link><pubDate>Thu, 29 Sep 2022 20:31:53 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;It’s been a while since I’ve used my Yealink MP56 Teams certified Desk Phone. I only bought it for testing purposes anyway… But today I noticed that the call control UI has been completely revamped.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I’m running Firmware Version 1449/1.0.94.2022090705/0907. (And yes, I used the awesome PowerToys Text Extractor (Win + Shift + T) to copy the text from the screenshot below.)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1GC3ucFmSDUefZHlDJh2Ig.jpeg"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="480"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1GC3ucFmSDUefZHlDJh2Ig_hu_dcd59f1e594dafdc.jpeg 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1GC3ucFmSDUefZHlDJh2Ig_hu_72b8b752068f20a2.jpeg 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="166"&#10; data-flex-basis="400px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;An incoming call now looks like this. If I remember correctly, the buttons used to be much smaller and located next to each other at the bottom of the screen.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1AegRntILpLiXhzwKM16Q.jpeg"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="480"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1AegRntILpLiXhzwKM16Q_hu_cba4289b6e60e0c.jpeg 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1AegRntILpLiXhzwKM16Q_hu_f241475218d5aeb4.jpeg 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="166"&#10; data-flex-basis="400px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The in-call controls also feature larger, centered buttons now.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1ukiZX9MRAIrIca4TTYAQ2Q.jpeg"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="480"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1ukiZX9MRAIrIca4TTYAQ2Q_hu_a8b7a9077720eafd.jpeg 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1ukiZX9MRAIrIca4TTYAQ2Q_hu_45e066b2d7058eb4.jpeg 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="166"&#10; data-flex-basis="400px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The transfer button has been moved to the main screen, which means that you’ll need one tap less to initiate a transfer now.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1Q3TrkssZ05qBSiENlfxM1w.jpeg"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="480"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1Q3TrkssZ05qBSiENlfxM1w_hu_e73d729651845ee2.jpeg 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1Q3TrkssZ05qBSiENlfxM1w_hu_9e4fd8bd7c4451a2.jpeg 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="166"&#10; data-flex-basis="400px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1fu0FAoGzkPiKzst5U9wfQ.jpeg"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="480"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1fu0FAoGzkPiKzst5U9wfQ_hu_da0465bdd3ac3804.jpeg 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1fu0FAoGzkPiKzst5U9wfQ_hu_8733add0a08fa6fd.jpeg 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="166"&#10; data-flex-basis="400px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The menu for the actual transfer / search looks the same in both the new and the old UI.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You can still bring back the old view by tapping &lt;strong&gt;…More&lt;/strong&gt;. and then &lt;strong&gt;Change view.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1zKuewvudu7c7RwrJgZKw.jpeg"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="480"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1zKuewvudu7c7RwrJgZKw_hu_f551a48f5455ea6d.jpeg 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1zKuewvudu7c7RwrJgZKw_hu_149031b4a342f77b.jpeg 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="166"&#10; data-flex-basis="400px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This will transition into the old UI where everything is located at the bottom of the screen.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1qE72elvoIwvZ26ObznmP1g.png"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="480"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1qE72elvoIwvZ26ObznmP1g_hu_904c8d5d75e6860d.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1qE72elvoIwvZ26ObznmP1g_hu_b1bb8c3e9849c8b5.png 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="166"&#10; data-flex-basis="400px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Funny enough, there’s no option to switch back to the new look once you’ve changed the view.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/17YI7KnZsSDfyPws1bdWHA.jpeg"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="480"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/17YI7KnZsSDfyPws1bdWHA_hu_ad77a694cda98b64.jpeg 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/17YI7KnZsSDfyPws1bdWHA_hu_5c68d60f31bcb553.jpeg 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="166"&#10; data-flex-basis="400px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The only way to get back to the new view is if you tap the &lt;strong&gt;←&lt;/strong&gt; arrow and then &lt;strong&gt;Tap to return to call.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1GekqCj551lsyzSTrdKAQg.png"&#10; width="800"&#10; height="97"&#10; srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1GekqCj551lsyzSTrdKAQg_hu_f6d6721827766c10.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/updated-calling-ui-on-teams-desk-phones-9e8f18790f5a/1GekqCj551lsyzSTrdKAQg_hu_7bfef62d5ae80bb9.png 1024w"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; &#10; &#10; class="gallery-image"&#10; data-flex-grow="824"&#10; data-flex-basis="1979px"&#10; &#10;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This will bring back the revamped UI for the active call. I suspect that the old UI will be removed entirely sooner or later. I don’t see any reason why one would need or want two different calling UIs. I also don’t think that Microsoft wants to maintain two different UIs. Especially if the new one features a lot of improvements and welcome changes.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Oh, and thanks to MVP James Cussen for the awesome &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.myteamslab.com/2020/10/teams-phone-screen-capture-tool.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&#10; &gt;Teams Phone Screen Capture Tool&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;</description></item></channel></rss>